"# Appendix G — Cortex recipes (real Motoi, not module-event queries)

The other dialect's Cortex recipes query an automatic stream of module events — `module-loaded`, `module-resolved`, `module-verified`, `module-call`. **Motoi emits none of those** (Chapter 13): there is no module system to instrument. It also binds none of the fancy query verbs the other dialect uses — `cortex/query-distinct`, `cortex/query-unused-imports`, `cortex/query-first`, and `cortex/query-diff` are all `error: unbound symbol`. What Motoi *does* have is `cortex/write` and `cortex/recall`, plus the whole standard library. This appendix rewrites each recipe using only those real tools: you record the fact, then compute over it with ordinary list verbs.

## Recipe 1 — What libraries did my program use?

You record it yourself as one fact:

```scheme
(cortex/write 'deps '(string list hash-table))
(cortex/recall 'deps)
;; ⇒ a memory record whose :data is (string list hash-table)
```

There is no automatic `module-loaded` list, because nothing loads modules. The honest dependency record is the one you write.

## Recipe 2 — Deduplicate a recorded list

The other dialect's `cortex/query-distinct` is, in Motoi, `delete-duplicates` over a list you kept:

```scheme
(delete-duplicates '(string string list hash-table list))
;; ⇒ (string list hash-table)
```

No special query verb — a standard SRFI-1 verb over your own data.

## Recipe 3 — Which recorded libraries went unused?

The other dialect's `cortex/query-unused-imports` has no basis here (no imports). You compute it: given everything you *had* and everything you *used*, the unused set is a set difference with `filter`/`member`:

```scheme
(define had  '(string list hash-table random))
(define used '(string list))
(filter (lambda (x) (not (member x used))) had)
;; ⇒ (hash-table random)
```

## Recipe 4 — Did my review pass?

The other dialect queried `module-verified`. Motoi has no verification event; you record your own judgement and read it back:

```scheme
(cortex/write 'review-ok #t)
(cortex/recall 'review-ok)
;; ⇒ a memory record whose :data is #t
```

## Recipe 5 — What did this component use?

Instead of per-cart `module-loaded`, key the fact by component name:

```scheme
(cortex/write 'component-a-deps '(string random))
(cortex/recall 'component-a-deps)
;; ⇒ a memory record whose :data is (string random)
```

## Recipe 6 — Latest value wins

`cortex/recall` returns the most recent write for a key — so \"what is the current value\" is free:

```scheme
(cortex/write 'current 'v1)
(cortex/write 'current 'v2)
(cortex/recall 'current)
;; ⇒ a memory record whose :data is v2
```

## Recipe 7 — Diff between two recorded snapshots

The other dialect's `cortex/query-diff` becomes two lists and a pair of set differences:

```scheme
(define before '(string list))
(define after  '(string hash-table))
(define added   (filter (lambda (x) (not (member x before))) after))
(define removed (filter (lambda (x) (not (member x after)))  before))
(list :added added :removed removed)
;; ⇒ (:added (hash-table) :removed (list))
```

That is a full added/removed diff, built from facts you kept and plain list verbs — no `query-diff` verb needed, because Motoi has none.

## Recipe 8 — A small audit report

Combine the recipes into one verb over your own recorded facts:

```scheme
(define (audit-report had used)
  (list :used     (delete-duplicates used)
        :unused   (filter (lambda (x) (not (member x used))) had)))

(audit-report '(string list hash-table random) '(string list list))
;; ⇒ (:used (string list) :unused (hash-table random))
```

Run it, save the output, compare against last time — the same discipline the other dialect's report gave, built without any module-event stream.

## Cortex is a memory, not a module tracker

Every recipe here writes a fact you chose to record and computes over it with standard verbs. That is the honest shape of \"auditing usage\" in Motoi: there is no automatic module telemetry (none of `cortex/query-distinct`, `cortex/query-unused-imports`, `cortex/query-first`, `cortex/query-diff` is bound), so you keep the facts you care about and reason over them yourself.

## Try this

Write a `deps` fact and recall it (Recipe 1). Dedup a list with `delete-duplicates` (Recipe 2). Compute an added/removed diff with `filter`/`member` (Recipe 7). Then confirm `cortex/query-diff` is `error: unbound symbol` — you did its job with two lists and a set difference, because Motoi has no module events to diff.")
